# Introduction # {#intro}

Web applications for audio production, live performance, and interactive education need to synchronize playback with other software and hardware instruments on the same local network.

Native music applications solve this problem using Ableton Link. Ableton Link is a peer-to-peer protocol over UDP multicast. It synchronizes tempo, beat position, and musical phase without a central master device.

This specification introduces the Web Tempo Sync API. The browser owns the local network sockets, handles peer discovery, and maintains clock synchronization. Web applications interact with high-level snapshot objects to schedule audio events and coordinate musical transport.

# Concepts # {#concepts}

## Sessions and Peers ## {#concept-session}

A <dfn>tempo session</dfn> represents a connection to a synchronized musical timeline shared among local network participants.

A <dfn>peer</dfn> is an independent network participant in the session. Participants can include digital audio workstations, mobile devices, hardware synthesizers, and web browser profiles.

To prevent local network flooding, a user agent exposes at most one logical peer per user profile. Multiple documents within the same user agent profile share the underlying session endpoint.

## Timelines, Beats, and Tempo ## {#concept-timeline}

A <dfn>timeline</dfn> maps points in continuous time to continuous musical beat coordinates.

<dfn>Tempo</dfn> is the rate of musical progress, measured in beats per minute (BPM). Tempo must be a positive finite floating-point number.

A <dfn>beat</dfn> is a continuous floating-point number indicating musical position. Integer values represent whole beat intervals (such as quarter notes in common time). Fractional values represent sub-beat subdivisions.

The relationship between time $t$ and beat $b$ on a linear timeline segment is:

$$b(t) = b_0 + (t - t_0) \times \frac{\text{tempo}}{60}$$

$$t(b) = t_0 + (b - b_0) \times \frac{60}{\text{tempo}}$$

Here $t_0$ is the reference time origin and $b_0$ is the reference beat origin.

## Quantum and Phase ## {#concept-quantum}

Musical structure is organized into recurring bars or measures.

The <dfn>quantum</dfn> is the number of beats in a musical measure. For example, 4/4 time has a quantum of 4.0 beats. 3/4 time has a quantum of 3.0 beats.

The <dfn>phase</dfn> represents the current position within the measure, defined over the half-open interval $[0, \text{quantum})$:

$$\text{phase}(t) = (b(t) \pmod{\text{quantum}} + \text{quantum}) \pmod{\text{quantum}}$$

Two devices share phase alignment when their beat grids align to the same bar boundaries.

## Host Time and Time Base Conversion ## {#concept-time-bases}

The underlying network sync engine operates on a monotonic system <dfn>host time</dfn>.

Web applications operate on two distinct browser time bases:
1. `performance.now()`: Monotonic document time in seconds, suitable for visual rendering.
2. `AudioContext.currentTime`: Audio rendering hardware time, measured in seconds from the audio hardware buffer timeline.

When an application captures session state, the user agent converts timeline parameters from [=host time=] into the requested time base.

# Navigator Extension # {#navigator-extension}

<xmp class="idl">
[SecureContext]
partial interface Navigator {
  readonly attribute TempoSync tempoSync;
};
</xmp>

The {{Navigator/tempoSync}} attribute returns the {{TempoSync}} instance associated with the current document.

# Interface `TempoSync` # {#interface-temposync}

<xmp class="idl">
interface TempoSync {
  Promise<TempoSession> requestSession(optional TempoSessionOptions options = {});
};

dictionary TempoSessionOptions {
  double quantum = 4;
  boolean startStopSync = false;
};
</xmp>

The {{TempoSync}} interface is the entry point for joining a tempo synchronization session.

## Methods ## {#temposync-methods}

<div algorithm="requestSession">
When the <dfn method for="TempoSync">requestSession(|options|)</dfn> method is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. Let |promise| be a new promise.
2. Let |document| be the current document.
3. If |document| is not a secure context, reject |promise| with a "{{SecurityError}}" {{DOMException}} and return |promise|.
4. If |document| is not [=allowed to use=] the [=policy-controlled feature=] `"tempo-sync"`, reject |promise| with a "{{SecurityError}}" {{DOMException}} and return |promise|.
5. If |options|["quantum"] is less than or equal to 0, or is not a finite number, reject |promise| with a {{RangeError}} and return |promise|.
6. Run the following steps in parallel:
  1. Let |permission| be the result of [=requesting permission to use=] `"tempo-sync"`.
  2. If |permission| is not `"granted"`, reject |promise| with a "{{NotAllowedError}}" {{DOMException}} and abort these steps.
  3. Let |session| be a newly created {{TempoSession}} instance initialized with |options|.
  4. Connect |session| to the user agent's shared tempo sync network endpoint.
  5. Resolve |promise| with |session|.
7. Return |promise|.

</div>

# Interface `TempoSession` # {#interface-temposession}

<xmp class="idl">
interface TempoSession : EventTarget {
  readonly attribute unsigned long numPeers;
  readonly attribute double quantum;
  TempoSessionState captureState(optional BaseAudioContext context);
  undefined commitState(TempoSessionState state);
  undefined close();
  attribute EventHandler onnumpeerschange;
  attribute EventHandler ontempochange;
  attribute EventHandler onplayingchange;
};
</xmp>

A {{TempoSession}} object is a document's connection to a [=tempo session=]: the shared musical [=timeline=].

## Attributes ## {#temposession-attributes}

* <dfn attribute for="TempoSession">numPeers</dfn>: Returns the number of other active [=peers=] discovered on the local network.
* <dfn attribute for="TempoSession">quantum</dfn>: Returns the default [=quantum=] specified when the session was created.
* <dfn attribute for="TempoSession">onnumpeerschange</dfn>: Event handler invoked when {{TempoSession/numPeers}} changes.
* <dfn attribute for="TempoSession">ontempochange</dfn>: Event handler invoked when the session tempo changes.
* <dfn attribute for="TempoSession">onplayingchange</dfn>: Event handler invoked when the shared start/stop transport state changes.

## Methods ## {#temposession-methods}

<div algorithm="captureState">
When the <dfn method for="TempoSession">captureState(|context|)</dfn> method is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If this {{TempoSession}} is closed, throw an "{{InvalidStateError}}" {{DOMException}}.
2. Let |snapshot| be a new {{TempoSessionState}} object.
3. Let |timeline| be the current internal network [=timeline=].
4. If |context| is provided:
  1. Let |timeBase| be |context|'s current hardware time in seconds.
  2. Map |timeline|'s host time coordinates into |context|'s time base using the audio clock filter.
5. If |context| is omitted:
  1. Let |timeBase| be `performance.now()` divided by 1000.0.
  2. Map |timeline|'s host time coordinates into document monotonic time in seconds.
6. Initialize |snapshot| with:
  * `tempo`: the current timeline tempo in BPM.
  * [=TempoSessionState/time origin=]: the mapped reference time origin.
  * [=TempoSessionState/beat origin=]: the reference beat coordinate at the time origin.
  * [=TempoSessionState/default quantum=]: this session's {{TempoSession/quantum}}.
  * `isPlaying`: the current transport playback state.
  * `timeForIsPlaying`: the mapped time when `isPlaying` was last toggled.
7. Return |snapshot|.

</div>

<div algorithm="commitState">
When the <dfn method for="TempoSession">commitState(|state|)</dfn> method is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If this {{TempoSession}} is closed, throw an "{{InvalidStateError}}" {{DOMException}}.
2. If |state| was not created by this {{TempoSession}}, throw an "{{InvalidModificationError}}" {{DOMException}}.
3. If |state| was already committed, throw an "{{InvalidStateError}}" {{DOMException}}.
4. Convert |state|'s time origins back to system host time.
5. Apply the modified timeline parameters to the internal network timeline.
6. Transmit update packets to local network peers.
7. Mark |state| as committed.

</div>

<div algorithm="close">
When the <dfn method for="TempoSession">close()</dfn> method is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If this {{TempoSession}} is already closed, return.
2. Mark this {{TempoSession}} as closed.
3. Detach this document from the underlying shared network session.
4. If no other active documents reference the shared session, shut down the local network socket.

</div>

# Interface `TempoSessionState` # {#interface-temposessionstate}

<xmp class="idl">
interface TempoSessionState {
  readonly attribute double tempo;
  undefined setTempo(double bpm, double atTime);
  double beatAtTime(double time, optional double quantum);
  double phaseAtTime(double time, optional double quantum);
  double timeAtBeat(double beat, optional double quantum);
  undefined requestBeatAtTime(double beat, double time, optional double quantum);
  undefined forceBeatAtTime(double beat, double time, optional double quantum);
  readonly attribute boolean isPlaying;
  readonly attribute double timeForIsPlaying;
  undefined setIsPlaying(boolean playing, double atTime);
};
</xmp>

A {{TempoSessionState}} instance is an immutable snapshot of the timeline at the moment of capture, unless modified through its mutation methods prior to committing.

## Internal slots ## {#temposessionstate-slots}

A {{TempoSessionState}} has these internal slots, set by {{TempoSession/captureState()}}:

* <dfn for="TempoSessionState">time origin</dfn>: a time, in the time base the state was captured in, that the [=TempoSessionState/beat origin=] is anchored to.
* <dfn for="TempoSessionState">beat origin</dfn>: the [=beat=] at the [=TempoSessionState/time origin=].
* <dfn for="TempoSessionState">default quantum</dfn>: the session's [=quantum=] when the state was captured, used when a method's `quantum` argument is omitted.

## Attributes ## {#temposessionstate-attributes}

* <dfn attribute for="TempoSessionState">tempo</dfn>: Returns the [=tempo=] in beats per minute.
* <dfn attribute for="TempoSessionState">isPlaying</dfn>: Returns true if the transport is playing, false otherwise.
* <dfn attribute for="TempoSessionState">timeForIsPlaying</dfn>: Returns the time at which `isPlaying` was last changed, in seconds.

## Methods ## {#temposessionstate-methods}

<div algorithm="setTempo">
When <dfn method for="TempoSessionState">setTempo(|bpm|, |atTime|)</dfn> is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If |bpm| is less than or equal to 0, or is not a finite number, throw a {{RangeError}}.
2. If |atTime| is not a finite number, throw a {{TypeError}}.
3. Let |currentBeat| be the result of invoking {{TempoSessionState/beatAtTime()}} with |atTime|.
4. Set this object's [=TempoSessionState/time origin=] to |atTime|.
5. Set this object's [=TempoSessionState/beat origin=] to |currentBeat|.
6. Set this object's tempo to |bpm|.

</div>

<div algorithm="beatAtTime">
When <dfn method for="TempoSessionState">beatAtTime(|time|, |quantum|)</dfn> is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If |time| is not a finite number, throw a {{TypeError}}.
2. Let |elapsed| be |time| minus this object's [=TempoSessionState/time origin=].
3. Let |beatsPerSecond| be this object's tempo divided by 60.0.
4. Let |beat| be this object's [=TempoSessionState/beat origin=] plus (|elapsed| * |beatsPerSecond|).
5. Return |beat|, the [=beat=] at |time|.

Issue: |quantum| is accepted for parity with Ableton Link, whose beat and time mappings keep each peer's beat values phase-aligned with the session for the quantum the caller uses. In this draft's single shared timeline it has no effect. Either specify that alignment or remove the argument.

</div>

<div algorithm="timeAtBeat">
When <dfn method for="TempoSessionState">timeAtBeat(|beat|, |quantum|)</dfn> is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If |beat| is not a finite number, throw a {{TypeError}}.
2. Let |beatDelta| be |beat| minus this object's [=TempoSessionState/beat origin=].
3. Let |secondsPerBeat| be 60.0 divided by this object's tempo.
4. Let |time| be this object's [=TempoSessionState/time origin=] plus (|beatDelta| * |secondsPerBeat|).
5. Return |time|.

Issue: |quantum| is accepted for parity with Ableton Link, whose beat and time mappings keep each peer's beat values phase-aligned with the session for the quantum the caller uses. In this draft's single shared timeline it has no effect. Either specify that alignment or remove the argument.

</div>

<div algorithm="phaseAtTime">
When <dfn method for="TempoSessionState">phaseAtTime(|time|, |quantum|)</dfn> is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If |time| is not a finite number, throw a {{TypeError}}.
2. Let |q| be |quantum| if provided and greater than 0, otherwise this object's [=TempoSessionState/default quantum=].
3. Let |beat| be the result of invoking {{TempoSessionState/beatAtTime()}} with |time|.
4. Let |rawPhase| be |beat| modulo |q|.
5. Return (|rawPhase| + |q|) modulo |q|, the [=phase=].

</div>

<div algorithm="requestBeatAtTime">
When <dfn method for="TempoSessionState">requestBeatAtTime(|beat|, |time|, |quantum|)</dfn> is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If |beat| or |time| is not a finite number, throw a {{TypeError}}.
2. Let |q| be |quantum| if provided and greater than 0, otherwise this object's [=TempoSessionState/default quantum=].
3. Let |currentBeat| be the result of invoking {{TempoSessionState/beatAtTime()}} with |time|.
4. Let |phaseDelta| be (|beat| - |currentBeat|) modulo |q|.
5. Set this object's [=TempoSessionState/time origin=] to |time|.
6. Set this object's [=TempoSessionState/beat origin=] to |currentBeat| + |phaseDelta|.

</div>

<div algorithm="forceBeatAtTime">
When <dfn method for="TempoSessionState">forceBeatAtTime(|beat|, |time|, |quantum|)</dfn> is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If |beat| or |time| is not a finite number, throw a {{TypeError}}.
2. Set this object's [=TempoSessionState/time origin=] to |time|.
3. Set this object's [=TempoSessionState/beat origin=] to |beat|.

Issue: |quantum| is accepted for parity with Ableton Link, whose beat and time mappings keep each peer's beat values phase-aligned with the session for the quantum the caller uses. In this draft's single shared timeline it has no effect. Either specify that alignment or remove the argument.

</div>

<div algorithm="setIsPlaying">
When <dfn method for="TempoSessionState">setIsPlaying(|playing|, |atTime|)</dfn> is invoked, the user agent MUST run these steps:

1. If |atTime| is not a finite number, throw a {{TypeError}}.
2. Set this object's `isPlaying` to |playing|.
3. Set this object's `timeForIsPlaying` to |atTime|.

</div>

# Permissions and Policy Integration # {#permissions-policy}

## Permissions Policy ## {#permissions-policy-integration}

This specification defines a [=policy-controlled feature=] identified by the string `"tempo-sync"`.

The default allowlist is `'self'`.

An iframe document cannot call {{TempoSync/requestSession()}} unless allowed by its container policy:

```html
<iframe src="https://synth.example.com" allow="tempo-sync"></iframe>
```

## Permissions API ## {#permissions-api-integration}

This specification defines a [=powerful feature=] whose [=powerful feature/name=] is `"tempo-sync"`.

* When granted, {{TempoSync/requestSession()}} succeeds without prompting.
* When denied, {{TempoSync/requestSession()}} immediately rejects with a "{{NotAllowedError}}" {{DOMException}}.
* When in prompt state, the user agent prompts the user with the origin of the document.

# Security and Privacy Considerations # {#security-privacy}

## Local Network Presence and Topology Leakage ## {#sec-local-network}

Joining an Ableton Link session involves sending UDP multicast packets on the local area network. Web applications could theoretically use this mechanism to infer the presence of local devices.

Mitigations:
1. **Explicit permission prompt**: The user agent MUST prompt the user before initiating any local network traffic.
2. **No address exposure**: The API exposes only the aggregate count of connected peers ({{TempoSession/numPeers}}). No IP addresses, port numbers, or device names are exposed to script.
3. **Single peer per profile**: The user agent joins as one logical peer. Internal tab topology cannot be fingerprinted by external peers.

## Cross-Origin Leakage ## {#sec-cross-origin}

The API is restricted to secure contexts (`[SecureContext]`) and top-level browsing contexts by default. Embedding in iframes requires an explicit `allow="tempo-sync"` directive.

## Multicast Flooding and Denial of Service ## {#sec-dos}

A compromised or malicious page could attempt to change tempo rapidly to degrade network performance or disrupt other music equipment.

The user agent MUST enforce rate limits on {{TempoSession/commitState()}}. Calls exceeding reasonable musical adjustment rates (for example, more than 20 commits per second) MUST be throttled or ignored.

# Acknowledgements # {#acknowledgements}

The authors thank the Ableton team for creating and open-sourcing the Ableton Link protocol. We also thank the Web Audio Working Group and the web music community for helpful discussions.

